  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bwindi Community Hospital  Project - live at Birth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda has one of the highest maternal and child death rates in the world. Less than half of deliveries take place with the help of a skilled health worker. This project aims to improve survival rates of mothers and their children in a poor, remote area in the South West corner of Uganda. It aims to increase access to maternal and child healthcare through community outreach and the introduction of an innovative health insurance scheme that promotes solidarity and collective action within communities. As a result, maternal and child death rates will be reduced, community members will have a greater awareness of the importance of family planning and birth control, and there will be better access to maternal and child health services for the poorest people.</narrative>
  </description>
